      "message": "When some modules call StatusBarManager.disable(DISABLE_NONE), unnecessary DisableRecord will be stacked. \n  mDisableRecords.size\u003d3\n    [0] barType\u003d0 userId\u003d0 what1\u003d0x00000000 what2\u003d0x00000000 pkg\u003dcom.android.systemui token\u003dandroid.os.BinderProxy@8dd7956\n    [1] barType\u003d0 userId\u003d0 what1\u003d0x00000000 what2\u003d0x00000000 pkg\u003dcom.LogiaGroup.LogiaDeck token\u003dandroid.os.BinderProxy@fc90dd7\n    [2] barType\u003d0 userId\u003d0 what1\u003d0x00000000 what2\u003d0x00000000 pkg\u003dcom.samsung.android.app.aodservice token\u003dandroid.os.BinderProxy@61c96c4\n\n\nOf course, it may be the module\u0027s fault, but if the module continues to call the following code, the records will continue to accumulate.\nmStatusBarManager \u003d (StatusBarManager) mContext.getSystemService(Context.STATUS_BAR_SERVICE);\nmStatusBarManager.disable(DISABLE_NONE)",
